Falsifies `device_tree_blob::verification::align4_rounds_up_to_a_multiple_of_four`.

The defect: `align4` rounds down instead of up, `n / 4 * 4` in place of `n.checked_add(3)` and a mask.
Both spellings type-check and both read as "the multiple of four near `n`"; only one of them is at
least `n`. Every caller uses this to skip a property's or a node's padding in the structure
block, so a floored `align4` would make the parser stop four bytes short of the next token for
any length that is not already a multiple of four, reading the tail of the current field as the
start of the next.

Expected to fail: the harness's own `assert!(a >= n)`, for any `n` not already a multiple of 4.
`a.is_multiple_of(4)` stays true under this defect (floor division still lands on a multiple of
four), which is why the harness needs all the assertions rather than the first one alone.

diff --git a/crates/device_tree_blob/src/lib.rs b/crates/device_tree_blob/src/lib.rs
index ed17aa9f6..2ee454348 100644
--- a/crates/device_tree_blob/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/device_tree_blob/src/lib.rs
@@ -1263,3 +1263,3 @@ struct Prop {
 fn align4(n: usize) -> Option<usize> {
-    n.checked_add(3).map(|up| up & !3)
+    Some(n / 4 * 4)
 }
